      "body": "## Overview\n\nThe Rust frontend returns a bare 404 for `/ping` and `/invocations`. The Python frontend always registers both for SageMaker (`vllm/entrypoints/serve/sagemaker/api_router.py`), and SageMaker health-checks a container through `/ping`, so a SageMaker deployment with `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1` never comes up healthy.\n\nThis serves `GET`/`POST /ping` with the existing `/health` handler, which is what Python does and what the Rust render server already does (`routes/render.rs`). `/invocations` gets the standard 501 placeholder the router uses for other Python routes it doesn't implement yet, so clients get a clear error instead of a 404.\n\nI found this by walking every path in the Python server's `/openapi.json` against both frontends running on the same engine. These were the only routes that 404 on Rust without a 501 placeholder or an open PR (`/generative_scoring` is #46427, `/v1/responses` is #58783).\n\n## Claims\n\n- `GET /ping` and `POST /ping` return the same status and empty body as `/health`: 200 while the engine is healthy, 503 after the engine core dies.\n- `POST /invocations` returns 501 `NotImplementedError` with the usual \"not supported by the Rust frontend yet\" message instead of 404.\n\n## Validation\n\nLive, `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` on the CPU engine, `vllm serve` with `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=0` vs `=1`, same flags:\n\n| Request | Python | Rust main `335dd77b09` | Rust this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /ping` | 200, empty | 404 | 200, empty |\n| `POST /ping` | 200, empty | 404 | 200, empty |\n| `POST /invocations` | 200 (routes to completions) | 404 | 501 |\n\nRoute tests (in-process, mock engine). The existing healthy and engine-dead `/health` tests now also cover `GET`/`POST /ping`, and `/invocations` is added to `unimplemented_python_routes_return_not_implemented`:\n\n```bash\ncd rust\ncargo test -p vllm-server --lib -- health_endpoint_returns unimplemented_python_routes_return_not_implemented\n# main + updated tests: 3 failed\n#   GET /ping: left 404, right 200 (and 503 in the engine-dead test)\n#   POST /invocations: left 404, right 501\n# this PR: 3 passed\ncargo test -p vllm-server   # 539 passed\n```\n\n`cargo fmt --check` clean, clippy adds no warnings in the changed files, pre-commit passes.\n\n## Details\n\n`/invocations` in Python picks the target endpoint by validating the body against each supported request type in turn. Porting that is a separate change, so I left a TODO next to the route instead of doing a partial version here.\n\nNo existing issue covers this. I checked open PRs touching `rust/src/server/src/routes.rs` and searched for `/ping`, `/invocations` and SageMaker in issues and PRs; none add these routes.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
